 "committedCopy": "The shoot ran with --same 1 and PASSED with 3,560,273 authored triangles removed and the Capitol dome visibly gone (0.172% and 0.308% of pixels). The same frames were then re-measured with --from --same 0.05, the tolerance derived from the measured day/golden floor of 0.000%, and the run goes RED: FAIL --same 0.05%, exit 1, both frames named, 'the sabotage moved 2 of 2 (pose, regime) frames past --same'. The verdict/remeasure blocks below are that second pass; the shoot's own settings are under `shoot`. Nothing was re-shot. ||| SIXTH PASS, 2026-09-20 -- RE-MEASURED, NOT RE-SHOT. The two Capitol poses' `wall` and `dome` rectangles were on MapLibre's own fill-extrusions, not on anything we author: `--break slopes` deleted 3,560,273 triangles and every measured number at both poses came back bit-identical. wall and dome are now read off the A-vs-B mask of that run (92-96% of each rectangle is pixels the sabotage changed by more than 3 of 255 on any channel; 86-91% at a threshold of 6), the old rectangles are kept as `downtown`/`flanking` and declared `basemap`, and every kept report was re-measured from its OWN frames with --from against the corrected night-routes.json. No frame in this file was taken again; the frames are byte-for-byte the ones the shoot produced. Capitol numbers before and after are tabulated in docs/night-implementation-plan.md sec W0a. Every shot also gained `frame.bytes`/`frame.sha1`, and `report.exit` now exists in all ten files. The measured consequence here: `wall` 71 -> 28 and `dome` 76 -> 20 at congress-30m, `wall` 72 -> 9 and `dome` 76 -> 6 at gate-1p7m, where before the re-aim NOTHING moved except `dome` at one pose. verdict.breakCoverage now carries movedMeasured/unmovedMeasured per pose.",
